  "summary": "Arg-e Bam is the walled earthen citadel of Bam in south-eastern Iran, within a World Heritage cultural landscape whose origins UNESCO traces to the Achaemenid period. It is described as a fortified medieval town built of mud layers. The earthquake of 26 December 2003 severely damaged or destroyed much of it.",
